  "question": {
    "text": "A capillary tube of radius $\\mathrm{r}$ is immersed vertically in a liquid such that liquid rises in it to height $\\mathrm{h}$ (less than the length of the tube). Mass of liquid in the capillary tube is $\\mathrm{m}$. If radius of the capillary tube is increased by $50 \\%$, then mass of liquid that will rise in the tube, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "85JX4",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3} \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Inh7i",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "209g5",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YqDbD",
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{4} \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{h}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~T} \\cos \\theta}{\\mathrm{r} \\rho \\mathrm{g}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{h} \\propto \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{r}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{h}_{2}}{\\mathrm{~h}_{1}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{r}_{1}}{\\mathrm{r}_{2}}=\\frac{2}{3}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\r\n\\left(\\because \\mathrm{r}_{1}=\\mathrm{r}, \\quad \\mathrm{r}_{2}\\right.&=\\mathrm{r}+50 \\% \\text { of } \\left.\\mathrm{r}=\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{r}\\right) \\\\\r\n\r\n\\text { New mass } \\mathrm{m}_{2}=\\pi \\mathrm{r}_{2}^{2} \\mathrm{~h}_{2} \\rho &=\\pi\\left(\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{r}_{1}\\right)^{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{3} \\mathrm{~h}_{1}\\right) \\rho \\\\\r\n\r\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_{1}^{2} \\mathrm{~h}_{1}\\right) \\rho=\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{~m}\r\n\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n\r\n$$",
